WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:04.300
Climate change is intensifying wildfires.

2
00:00:04.600 --> 00:00:09.300
Every year, droughts last longer
and the heat grows stronger.

3
00:00:09.900 --> 00:00:14.000
In Latin America, wildfires are spreading
faster and faster,

4
00:00:14.100 --> 00:00:18.700
and in just a few minutes,
fire can transform our landscape.

5
00:00:18.900 --> 00:00:23.900
Smoke travels, crossing rivers,
towns, and rainforests.

6
00:00:24.200 --> 00:00:27.300
And the air we breathe changes
without us even noticing.

7
00:00:27.500 --> 00:00:30.200
Fire knows no borders.

8
00:00:30.500 --> 00:00:34.200
The air moves and carries pollution
from one country to another.

9
00:00:34.300 --> 00:00:38.400
Wildfires are no longer a distant problem.

10
00:00:38.700 --> 00:00:44.200
Their smoke reaches our cities,
our homes, and our lungs.

11
00:00:44.400 --> 00:00:46.900
However, it's not too late.

12
00:00:47.300 --> 00:00:53.300
Most wildfires start with agricultural burning
that we can manage.

13
00:00:53.700 --> 00:00:56.700
With training and burning calendars,
fire can be controlled.

14
00:00:56.800 --> 00:01:02.900
And when it gets out of control, an early warning system
can keep it from becoming a disaster.

15
00:01:03.000 --> 00:01:09.700
The health of millions of people is at risk
due to rising wildfires and air pollution.

16
00:01:09.800 --> 00:01:16.500
At Lancet Countdown, we bring together researchers
from across the region to understand and act on this crisis.

17
00:01:16.900 --> 00:01:20.200
Our future depends on what we do today.
